een  hard hit by the covet economy shouldn't  he keep those promises  well i think that americans actually  separate out the relief from  the need for coveted monies which we all  need and we all are going to  agree on that but some of these other  things are pretty incredible a friend of  mine said it's like the biden  administration  looked through the twitter feed of the  far left and just picked out a whole  bunch of random things and put them  together  um two things on the pipeline um jesse  did you know that even the canadians  say that it will meet their it will  allow them to meet  their uh greenhouse gas emissions  reductions so if the canadians  are okay with it surely americans should  be able to be okay with it  the other thing is the idea of doing the  15 an hour minimum wage  okay if you want to do that fine but  that would mean ignoring the  congressional budget office that says  that um 3.7 million jobs could be lost  because of that  there are um yes elections have  consequences but so do some of these  policies  so greg part of this is the use of  executive  orders uh biden says he's going to use  executive orders to do  things and you know rejoin the climate  deal and the like  but isn't that a response to the fact  that president trump  used executive orders to undo a lot of  what obama had done  that's you're absolutely right that's  the problem with executive orders  is that they can be done and then they  could be undone it's the post-election  ritual right  but in this case it's something else  it's a retribution strategy  i'm gonna coin a phrase they're throwing  the baby out  with the bath water because they hate  trump so much  they are willing to undo all of the  positive things that even they secretly  admit  were positive building a strong economy  the increased wages the trade  transparency  the relationship with north korea the  peace agreements in the middle east  the cheap energy they are so vindictive  and not just about trump but